\begin{remark}[Consistent parameter selection via spatial stiffness]
\label{rem:consistent-params}
Corollaries~\ref{cor:local-error-pruning}, \ref{cor:flux-timestep}, and~\ref{cor:expansion-depth} and Remark~\ref{rem:expansion-strategy} provide a self-consistent framework for parameter selection, governed by the spatial stiffness ratio $\kappa=\lambda_{\max}/\Phi_{\mathrm{total}}$:
\begin{itemize}
  \item \textbf{Time step:} use the total-flux rule $\Delta t = \varepsilon_{\Delta t}/\Phi_{\mathrm{total}}$ (leading-order error $\lesssim\varepsilon_{\Delta t}$, $\mu=\kappa\,\varepsilon_{\Delta t}$); for highly stiff systems apply the max-propensity cap (Remark~\ref{rem:max-propensity-cap}) to enforce $\mu\leq 1$ unconditionally \hfill (Corollary~\ref{cor:flux-timestep}),
  \item \textbf{Expansion depth and strategy:} use $d=1$ (ensured by $\kappa\,\varepsilon_{\Delta t}\leq 1$ or the cap); choose SSA expansion when $\kappa\approx 1$ (one dominant channel) and stoichiometric expansion when $\kappa>1$ \hfill (Corollary~\ref{cor:expansion-depth}, Remark~\ref{rem:expansion-strategy}),
  \item \textbf{Flux tolerance:} $\varepsilon_{\mathrm{flux}} \ll \varepsilon_{\Delta t}$, e.g., $\varepsilon_{\mathrm{flux}} = \varepsilon_{\Delta t}/w_{\max}$ \hfill (Corollary~\ref{cor:local-error-pruning}).
\end{itemize}
\end{remark}

