\begin{remark}[Unified parameter selection]
\label{rem:consistent-params}
The single criterion $\Phi_{\mathrm{out}}\,\Delta t \leq \varepsilon_{\Delta t}$ governs all three algorithm components (Remark~\ref{rem:phiout-central}).  Parameters follow from choosing how to split the error budget between spatial and temporal accuracy:
\begin{itemize}
  \item \textbf{Expansion strategy and depth:} choose the strategy that achieves the desired $\Phi_{\mathrm{out}}/\Phi_{\mathrm{total}}$ ratio within the state-space budget (Remark~\ref{rem:expansion-strategy}); use $d=1$ (guaranteed when $\kappa\,\varepsilon_{\Delta t}\leq 1$, or enforced by the max-propensity cap, Corollary~\ref{cor:expansion-depth}).
